;; world/rooms/wrongwater/x-2y7.room
(room
  region: wrongwater
  at: (-2 7)
  title: "Under the Well"
  intent: "you drop onto dry ground, and the water you came through hangs overhead with its surface facing down: a breath"
  bed: (air 0.15 water 0.5 hang 0.35 drone 0.6)
  light: 0.6
  grid:
  ("############### #########"
   "###############+#~~~~~###"
   "####    ####    #~~~~~# #"
   "###                     #"
   "##                      #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                        "
   "#                        "
   "##%  %###################"
   "##%  %###################")
  decor: auto)
;; The crack under the Ice Well's rising drip comes in at (15,0), one cell
;; wide. The drip door sits at its foot, (15,1), inside this room, off the
;; seam (a shut door is solid; a solid cell against an open one fails the
;; seam check). STUB until SYSTEMS lands the stillness door
;; (tasks/harkfell-depths-systems): (15,1) is a + (air drawn as rock), so the
;; door is open in every carry set, which is what the checker assumes for
;; the real door. The landing (row 8) is seven rows under the door: the
;; crack cannot be reached again from here. A small lake hangs in a ceiling
;; pocket east of the crack (17-21, rows 1-2), out of every jump's reach: a
;; picture. East to the Hanging Tarn (rows 7-8); down the rough shaft (3-4)
;; to the Upward Grove, whose rough walls are the climb back.
